Up until a couple of weeks ago, I had never really tried protection
racket. Now I've tested it and have had a 100% success rate thus far,
though only with three characters (2 x gnomish healer, 1 x human
ranger). I now think that it is a good bet for some characters. The
gnomish healers are the simplest example where I think not doing it is
worse for survival.

With the ranger I decided to adopt racket when I found a magic whistle
on the first level. This combined with the 2nd level wand shop
containing two wands of fire enabled me to reach Minetown without any
real danger. 

So, from now on, my advice will be: Do the protection racket when you
have a reason to believe that it will increase the chances of survival
for that particular character.

